+## Request 24: Dashboard
+**Status**: ✅ Completed and tested
+
+### What was done
+- Added `dashboard(invoices, asOf)` function to src/reports.js
+- Returns comprehensive metrics object with:
+  - `counts`: Object with invoice counts by status (draft, issued, partially_paid, paid)
+  - `outstanding`: Total amount due on invoices with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'
+  - `overdue`: Object with { count, amount } from overdueInvoices
+  - `topCustomers`: Array of top 3 customers by amount due, as [{ customerId, due }], sorted highest first
+- Dashboard aggregates data from multiple sources:
+  - Uses balanceDue() to calculate amounts due per invoice
+  - Uses overdueInvoices() to identify and sum overdue amounts
+  - Tracks customer totals across invoices
+- Added 9 comprehensive tests to test/reports.test.js covering:
+  - Empty invoices array
+  - Status counting
+  - Outstanding calculation
+  - Overdue identification and calculation
+  - Top customers ranking
+  - Draft and paid invoice exclusion
+  - Partially paid invoice handling
+  - Null invoice graceful handling
+
+### Implementation details
+- Draft and paid invoices excluded from outstanding calculation
+- Partially paid invoices included in outstanding (with balance due amount)
+- Top customers limited to top 3, sorted by descending amount due
+- Overdue amount calculated from overdueInvoices results
+- All 9 dashboard tests passing
